[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2860226510","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106151#issuecomment-2860226510","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106151","id":2860226510,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qe5fO","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T20:17:37Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T20:19:43Z","body":"I wonder if this is the proper fix, or is it just working around the underlying problem?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/717df3ee883d59ee5df036d95109009f3488b64c/scene/gui/tab_bar.cpp#L201-L212\r\n\r\nTab bar's close button logic explicitly filters out the `-1` index, but the `close_with_middle_mouse` case does not. Maybe it should?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlso some callers to `_scene_tab_closed` have an error check via `ERR_FAIL_COND(tab_idx < 0);` prepended. Maybe that can be moved into where you're currently doing an early return, since the `_scene_tab_closed` method should never be called with negative values.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2860226510/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861062678","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106151#issuecomment-2861062678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106151","id":2861062678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qiFoW","user":{"login":"SaNeOr","id":22307698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzA3Njk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22307698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr","html_url":"https://github.com/SaNeOr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SaNeOr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-08T01:04:24Z","updated_at":"2025-05-08T01:04:24Z","body":"> Also some callers to `_scene_tab_closed` have an error check via `ERR_FAIL_COND(tab_idx < 0);` prepended. Maybe that can be moved into where you're currently doing an early return, since the `_scene_tab_closed` method should never be called with negative values.\r\n\r\nIndeed, it should be so. I’ve adjusted the fix accordingly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2861062678/reactions","total_count":1,"+1